# Agent review routing

After a non-trivial implementation (not a one-line copy change), run the matching reviewers before claiming done. Do not skip because the same model wrote the code.

| Change | Subagent |
|--------|----------|
| `.ts` / `.tsx` types, async, APIs | `typescript-reviewer` |
| React components, hooks, RSC/client boundaries | `react-reviewer` |
| `src/components/three/**`, comet-card, Orby canvas | `three-artist` |
| Auth, cookies, env, routes, CSP, rate limits | `security-reviewer` |
| Interactive UI, focus, keyboard, contrast | `a11y-architect` |
| After code lands, before "done" | `portfolio-verify` |
| Sanity schema/query/content UI | `portfolio-cms` |
| Layout/visual polish only | `portfolio-polish` |

On pull requests, Bugbot is the GitHub reviewer. In chat, `/review-bugbot` and `/review-security` are allowed when the user asks.

Do not add ESLint. Use `pnpm lint` (Biome), `pnpm typecheck`, and `pnpm test` as the mechanical bar.
